      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-58655",
      ":question/problem": "In a dog kennel, $20$ dogs eat $60$ treats each day. If we want to determine the number of treats that each dog eats on average, we use the formula $A = \\frac{n}{d}$, where $n$ represents the total of treats while $d$ represents the total number of dogs.\n\nFind an appropriate measurement unit for $A$."
